# =============================================================================
# PlungeWise — HTTP security headers (Netlify `_headers`)
# Task:    PW-SECURITY-BASELINE-001
# Created: 2026-07-27
# Docs:    docs/SECURITY_BASELINE.md
#
# READ BEFORE EDITING
#
# 1. The Content Security Policy below is REPORT-ONLY. It blocks nothing.
#    Violations appear only in the browser console (DevTools > Console),
#    because the site has no backend and therefore no report endpoint.
#    Do NOT rename `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only` to
#    `Content-Security-Policy` without explicit written approval.
#
# 2. `frame-ancestors` is NOT enforced while the policy is Report-Only.
#    `X-Frame-Options: DENY` is what actually blocks clickjacking today.
#    It can be removed on the day the CSP becomes enforced.
#
# 3. The policy is deliberately written to match the real inventory of the
#    site: zero external scripts, zero external stylesheets, zero external
#    fonts, zero external images, zero iframes, zero network calls.
#    A clean policy is a tripwire — if anything ever starts reporting,
#    something changed that should not have.
#
# 4. GA4 was connected on 2026-07-28 (PW-GA4-001) and this policy was widened
#    for it. Only three Google hosts were added — the tag loader, the
#    measurement endpoints, and the reporting endpoint:
#
#      script-src   https://www.googletagmanager.com
#      img-src      https://*.google-analytics.com https://www.googletagmanager.com
#      connect-src  https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com
#                   https://www.googletagmanager.com
#
#    Google's own CSP guide also lists doubleclick.net, google.com and
#    googlesyndication.com. Those are for Google Signals and Google Ads
#    features. This site runs neither, so they are deliberately LEFT OUT: an
#    advertising host in the policy would silence exactly the report we want
#    to see if advertising features are ever switched on by accident. If a
#    violation for one of them ever appears, that is information, not a bug —
#    check the GA4 property settings before widening.
#    See docs/SECURITY_BASELINE.md, section "GA4".
#
# Netlify syntax: a path pattern on its own line, then header lines indented
# by two spaces. Blank lines separate blocks. `#` starts a comment.
# =============================================================================

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), screen-wake-lock=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
